# Velt API credentials (required)
NEXT_PUBLIC_VELT_API_KEY=your_api_key
VELT_AUTH_TOKEN=your_auth_token

# Optional: self-hosted comment backend (leave unset for this demo)
# When set, comment reads/writes go to Django instead of Velt cloud.
# Agent comments seeded via REST API require Velt cloud unless you mirror them.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SELF_HOSTING_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000/api/velt

# Optional: permission provider auth (production)
# VELT_PERMISSION_PROVIDER_TOKEN=your_permission_provider_token

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Velt Console configuration (required — cannot be set in code)
# https://console.velt.dev
#
# This demo reproduces a customer configuration that layers several access
# features together. For it to behave correctly, configure the API key above:
#
#   1. Require JWT Token: ON
#      https://console.velt.dev/dashboard/config/general
#
#   2. Default Document Access Type: organizationPrivate
#      https://console.velt.dev/dashboard/config/appconfig
#      (Only same-org users can access a resource; cross-org users need an
#       explicit grant — which is why User 2/4 rely on the Permission Provider.)
#
#   3. Real-Time Permission Provider: ENABLED
#      https://console.velt.dev/dashboard/config/permission-provider
#      - Local dev: the browser dev resolver is used (permissionProvider.dev:true
#        in app/page.tsx), so no tunnel is needed. Works on DEV/TEST keys only.
#      - Production: register the public HTTPS URL of
#        /api/velt/check-permissions here (dev resolver is ignored for prod keys).
#      NOTE: the RTPP must be ENABLED for permissions to be gated at all; the dev
#      resolver only changes WHERE the check runs, not WHETHER it runs.
#
#   4. Private Comments (beta): ENABLED
#      Required for the visibility banner (public / organization-private /
#      restricted) rendered by <VeltComments visibilityOptions />.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
